#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:5
#: 0f6970012f5843f1ba27107d620809be
msgid "Passing Serial over DroneCAN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:7
#: fa8328cc6b294a52af2a13a166fddcec
msgid "It is possible to pass serial communications from programs such as Ublox GPS U-Center over DroneCAN to the peripheral. This allows configuring and firmware updating internal serially connected peripherals sitting behind a DroneCAN interface, such as GPS modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:9
#: 8a8d755401514fc28ec39bc0a8e7169c
msgid "The DroneCAN peripheral must be running AP_Periph firmware revision 1.5.1 or later and the DroneCAN GUI tool version 1.2.22 or later"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:11
#: 59fd197214ae49f3a83fbceb75defa5b
msgid "This is accomplished using the latest version of the `DroneCAN GUI tool <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/CAN_GUI/>`__ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:13
#: bfc15ca1afa2475f8136efc7122e2df3
msgid "Connect the autopilot with its target DroneCAN peripheral to your PC. Do not start a local ground station like Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:14
#: eedca2b5e4f544d28044e40b7d871227
msgid "Start the DroneCAN GUI tool over MAVlink to the autopilot and click the local node ID checkmark"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:19
#: 0be049a02cbc426598c3864b159a6535
msgid "Click Panels->Serial Forwarding and select the peripheral node to forward from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:24
#: 9f8105d5dfac4fd89855681baca90483
msgid "Start U-Center or other appropriate tool and connect to the local host using port 2001, ie 127.0.0.1:2001 from its Receiver->Connection->Network Connection menu. You may have to create it as a NEW connection first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:29
#: 6554e7a87e21488fb398b736ba21bb2b
msgid "You will now be connected to the application and the State in the Serial Forwarding dialog will change to show the connection. You can examine the DroneCAN module's data flow, check its firmware revision, make configuration changes, etc. Whatever you could do if the module was directly connected to the PCs serial port using U-Center or other application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:31
#: 4800c3dcc4d94c7ab31de2481592dbdc
msgid "In order to change configuration of the DroneCAN's peripheral module (GPS,etc.) over this link you will need to change \"UART Locking\" in the Serial Forwarding dialog to \"Locked\". This gives the connected program exclusive access to the module to allow changes to be made without the DroneCAN peripheral's microcontroller overwriting them. This is required to make permanent configuration changes and for firmware upgrading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:33
#: 90da8779e6da4e8db91b6c9be3f1a95f
msgid "be aware that configuration changes you make may still be overwritten when rebooting the DroneCAN peripheral. For example, some GPS configuration items are changed at initialization of a GPS unless the :ref:`GPS_AUTO_CONFIG<GPS_AUTO_CONFIG>` is disabled, but those not auto configured would remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:36
#: de04c9d9b577473ca092158f8678dace
msgid "Firmware Update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:38
#: 9e8acd9327764da99e5f2cd0ff5e2162
msgid "this has only been tested on Ublox F9P based devices as of this writing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:40
#: de658a60c8744917a9b13b9f9f319463
msgid "While in the above connected state, you can also update the internal module's firmware, if available and if the module normally allows this when connected as a standalone module, outside of the DroneCAN peripheral."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:42
#: f74ceefbbeb04934a7afc12fc60f3638
msgid "For UBlox F9P GPSs, you will need to change the modules baud rate from 230.4KBaud down to 56.7Kbaud using the Config-> PRT configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:44
#: 41de2e7106d74773aba5c373baf372a9
msgid "Check the uBlox message handling checkbox in the Serial Forwarding dialog box. This will watch for the baud rate change you will be making and change the DroneCAN's serial port baud rate to match so communication can continue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:45
#: bb5789656ef54b48aa9ebc80ba67ef67
msgid "Select View->Configuration->PRT and change the baud to 57.6K and click the send button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:50
#: 7447295f6fd248d18242013c8d7a0893
msgid "Verify that communication is still occurring by seeing the RX bytes number change in the Serial Forwarding dialog box. If not repeat the about PRT change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-over-DroneCAN.rst:51
#: efe4f935b19146c696015d6ff9dbbb76
msgid "Then using U-Center's Tools menu, select the Firmware update and select the firmware image file and set the baud rate to 56.7Kbaud. Click GO button at the bottom  to start the update."
msgstr ""

